  urldate = {2026-10-20},
  abstract = {NoSQL database systems offer powerful advantages for managing geospatial dataset. Their flexible schema design allows seamless integration of diverse spatial formats such as GeoJSON and many more. Unlike traditional relational databases, NoSQL platforms scale horizontally and support real-time data ingestion and querying. Built-in geospatial functions and indexing enable efficient spatial analysis and location-based services. As geodata continues to grow in volume and complexity, NoSQL provides a dynamic and scalable foundation for innovative geospatial solutions. This material includes the following topics: a brief overview on the Geodata Management in the Context of ``Big Data'' , when to decide for NoSQL, What are the supports for spatial data?},
